From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:09:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compact retained layouts and break lines from a summary

Compact retained Parley layouts: style metrics, inline boxes and other buffers drop
their growth slack once a layout is built and mostly empty buffers become thin
vectors, laid-out underline and strikethrough decorations are boxed, shaped clusters
store only the start of their characters and read positions, styles, character
ranges and grapheme starts through the shaped text, and a build reuses the last
resolved font family. Layout and paint output are unchanged.

Break lines from a summary of a layout's break segments: the summary carries
widths, break opportunities, inline boxes and indent, so an embedder that evicts a
laid-out paragraph can break and measure it again without reshaping, including
pre-wrap text, top and bottom aligned spans and paragraphs with absolutely
positioned boxes, and the text indent a layout was last given is exposed. Breaking
from a summary yields the same lines as breaking the shaped layout.
